# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF
# on the way to disk. The line-ending analyzer then fails the whole build on the
# Windows leg while the Linux and macOS legs pass, because the files on disk no
# longer match what is in the repository. `eol=lf` pins the checkout, so the
# working tree matches the index everywhere.
#
# The .editorconfig already sets end_of_line = lf for editors; this is the same
# rule for git, which editors do not control.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise binary content — a stray LF-to-CRLF pass corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.snk binary
*.pfx binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
